# Senior Associate – People in Deals (PiD)

London

 Senior Associate

Apply now

Job ID

755458WD

Contract Type

Full time

Line Of Service

Deals

**About the role**

People in Deals (PiD) is a market leading team sitting within PwC’s M&A Operations Deals business, advising both corporate and private equity clients across the M&A (merger & acquisitions) cycle, including integration, and with longer term transformation. Our clients include some of the most well-known brands and businesses, who understand that putting people at the heart of any M&A activity is critical to achieving deal value.

Our PiD team assists clients with the operational aspects of a transaction relating to the workforce to identify key risks and opportunities, including but not limited to:

* HR & People Separation;

* Employee relations & consultation;

* Culture, Comms & Change;

* TOM (Target Operating Model) & Org Design;

* Reward separation & harmonisation;

* Talent management and skills agenda;

* HR Function design.

As a Senior Associate in the PiD team, you’ll be at the heart of our delivery on some of the most complex and high-profile transactions in the market. You will work closely with colleagues on delivery of client engagements, supporting key workstreams. Drawing on your people expertise, you’ll help organisations navigate critical workforce challenges across the deal lifecycle — from planning and execution to integration and transformation.

.

You’ll be part of a close-knit, high-performing team where you will take ownership of deliverables, provide expertise on workforce-related issues, liaise with clients, and act as a coach and mentor to more junior colleagues.

**What your days will look like:**

* Building and maintaining trusted relationships with People leaders and other senior business stakeholders;

* Managing workstream delivery to time, quality, and budget, while providing insight and lessons learned from previous projects;

* Coaching and developing colleagues at all levels, providing feedback and guidance to enhance technical, interpersonal, and consulting skills across the team;

* Working with cross-functional PwC teams to bring integrated solutions to client challenges;

* Driving business development by scoping people related activities on transactions, contributing to proposals, and shaping compelling client propositions;

* Supporting the development of our practice through thought leadership, knowledge sharing, and sector-specific initiatives.

**This role is for you if:**

* Proven success in leading workstream delivery, managing priorities, and producing high-quality outputs under the pressures of a deal environment;

* Experience in consulting or professional services would be advantageous, but not essential.
* Ability to leverage AI and digital tools to enhance analysis, improve efficiency, and deliver innovative solutions to clients.
* Strong analytical skills and data literacy; proficiency in Excel, Power BI, or other data tools is preferred;
* Experience in coaching, mentoring, and performance managing teams to support with the continuous improvement of capability and performance;
* Some experience of working on deals (integration, carve-out, or post-deal), ideally combined with broader business transformation experience and a strong people focused background;
* Strong stakeholder management skills, with the ability to engage credibly with senior leaders and manage upwards effectively;

**What you’ll receive from us:**

No matter where you may be in your career or personal life, our benefits are designed to add value and support, recognising and rewarding you fairly for your contributions.

We offer a range of benefits including empowered flexibility and a working week split between office, home and client site; private medical cover and 24/7 access to a qualified virtual GP; six volunteering days a year and much more.

Why Deals?



In Deals we solve the important problems that stand in the way of value being created, sustained, realised or protected for our clients – working together to aid responsible recovery and growth. Working on iconic deals with national and global clients, we put together major mergers and acquisitions and resolve business crises - from international take-over bids to financial crime investigations and cases of insolvency. We draw upon our deals experience across many industries to support and partner with our clients, to positively impact society and the communities in which we operate.

Apply now

# Aquatic Ecologist | Expression Of Interest

## Cambridge, GBR

**Join our** **Freshwater** **Aquatic** **Ecology** **Team**

We are growing our Freshwater Aquatic Ecology team and are looking to connect with talented aquatic ecologists who are passionate about protecting, enhancing and restoring freshwater environments across the UK and Ireland.

We welcome expressions of interest from aquatic ecologists across all grades, from Consultant through to Senior Principal. Whether you are looking to develop your technical expertise or seeking an opportunity to help shape the future direction of a growing team, we would love to hear from you.

You will work on nationally significant and technically challenging projects, collaborate with a supportive and multidisciplinary team, and help clients deliver sustainable development while protecting and enhancing the freshwater environment.

As our team continues to grow organically, there are opportunities to influence technical capability, mentoring, service development and the delivery of projects across the UK and Ireland. We are committed to creating an environment where people are supported to grow, develop technical specialisms and pursue their own professional interests whilst contributing to the success of the wider team.

We are proud of the collaborative and supportive culture we have built, where knowledge sharing, teamwork and professional development are valued alongside technical excellence.

Working alongside regional and national technical leaders, you will play a key role in delivering freshwater aquatic ecology expertise across a diverse portfolio of projects, supporting clients from the earliest stages of planning and survey design through to environmental assessment, project delivery and long-term monitoring.

**We are actively interested in speaking with candidates across multiple grades and locations throughout the UK and Ireland and recognise that** **great talent** **can come from any location**

**What** **You’ll** **Be Working On**

Our team supports a varied portfolio of work across the water, energy, infrastructure and development sectors, including:

* Strategic water resource and drought resilience schemes;
* Nationally significant infrastructure projects;
* River restoration and nature recovery initiatives;
* Fisheries and fish passage assessments;
* Water Framework Directive (WFD) assessments;
* Freshwater ecological monitoring programmes;
* Hydropower and renewable energy developments; and
* Ecological and environmental impact assessments.

No two projects are the same. Your work will directly contribute to understanding, protecting, enhancing and restoring rivers, lakes, reservoirs, canals and other freshwater habitats.

You will also have opportunities to collaborate with specialists across ecology, hydrology, hydrogeology, geomorphology, hydraulic modelling, environmental planning and engineering, providing integrated solutions to complex environmental challenges.

**About You**

We are looking for passionate aquatic ecology professionals with consultancy, regulatory, academic or industry experience.

**You’ll** **have:**

* A degree in Aquatic Ecology, Ecology, Environmental Science, Fisheries Science or a related discipline;
* Membership of a relevant professional body (e.g. CIEEM, IFM or CIWEM), with chartered status desirable for more senior roles, or a willingness to work towards professional accreditation;
* Experience undertaking, managing or interpreting freshwater ecological surveys and assessments;
* Knowledge of relevant environmental legislation, planning policy and regulatory frameworks applicable to the jurisdictions in which you work;
* Experience in one or more areas of freshwater ecology, which may include:
* Fish, macrophyte, macroinvertebrate or diatom surveys and assessments;
* Fish passage and barrier assessments;
* Aquatic habitat surveys and assessments (e.g. habitat walkovers, RHS, RCA and MoRPh);
* Hydroecology and environmental flows;
* River restoration and nature-based solutions;
* Ecological and Environmental Impact Assessment, including EcIA, EIA and Environmental Statement inputs;
* Habitats Regulations Assessment (HRA) or equivalent; or
* WFD assessment and compliance;
* The ability to undertake technical reporting and communicate scientific information clearly and accurately;
* Strong written and verbal communication skills; and
* The ability to contribute to project delivery, client relationships and technical guidance at a level appropriate to your experience.

**For Principal and Senior Principal grades, we would also welcome experience in:**

* Providing technical leadership and mentoring;
* Designing and managing freshwater survey and monitoring programmes;
* Managing projects, programmes, budgets and multidisciplinary workstreams;
* Developing and maintaining strong client and regulatory relationships;
* Supporting business development and preparing technical and commercial proposals;
* Undertaking technical review and quality assurance;
* Leading complex environmental assessments; and
* Supporting the growth and development of technical services and team capability.

**If your experience does not tick every box, we still encourage you to apply. We hire people, not checklists**

**Particular Areas** **of Interest**

While we are keen to hear from aquatic ecologists with a broad range of skills and experience, we are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in one or both of the following areas:

* **Macrophyte survey,** **assessment** **and reporting** , including macrophyte identification, application of WFD survey methodologies, and interpretation of LEAFPACS outputs for ecological classification and assessment; and
* **Aquatic ecological data analysis using R** , including data management, statistical analysis, data visualisation, reproducible workflows and the interpretation of freshwater ecological datasets.

Experience in either of these areas is not essential for all roles. We welcome expressions of interest from candidates with strengths across the wider aquatic ecology discipline.

**Why Join Us**

* We put people first: We're proud of our friendly, inclusive and collaborative environment where everyone feels valued and driven to succeed.
* We are driven to achieve: Named in the top 50 companies to work by Glassdoor 2025. Recognised by Corporate Knights as one of the world's top 10 most sustainable companies in 2025. Named 'Best Place to Work' and 'International Consulting Firm of the Year' at the NCE Awards 2024.
* We do what is right: Industry-leading training and development, as well as paid professional subscriptions. A professional progression plan, supporting you to become chartered.
* We are better together: A supportive and collaborative team environment and Early Careers peer group, and a wider ERG network (see more on our ERGs here: Stantec Employee Resource Groups)
* Growth: We're on an exciting growth journey across the UK - we want you to be part of it!
* Great Benefits: Competitive salary, bonus schemes, enhanced pension plan, annual leave with the option to buy/sell additional days, private medical insurance, group income protection & life assurance included as standard, as well as discounted gym membership and lots more.
* Hybrid / Flexible working: Enjoy a healthy work-life balance with our hybrid approach.

#UKWater #LI-MH1

**About Stantec**

The Stantec community unites more than 34,000 employees working in over 450 locations across 6 continents. We have been working with our clients and communities in the UK for over 150 years. We plan, design, deliver and manage the development and infrastructure needed to support the creation of sustainable, healthy and prosperous communities.

Our teams provide effective and relevant solutions, translating our clients’ vision into valued consents, deliverable plans for projects and programmes, and efficient designs for delivery, based on technical excellence and deep market insights. We deal with today’s challenges, but also keep a fairer, better tomorrow in sight, looking at how we deliver clean growth, support radical changes in our economy and meet the needs of future communities.

Stantec provides equal employment opportunities to all qualified employees and applicants for future and current employment and prohibit discrimination on the grounds of race, colour, religion, sex, national origin, age, marital status, genetic information, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or gender expression. We prohibit discrimination in decisions concerning recruitment, hiring, referral, promotion, compensation, fringe benefits, job training, terminations or any other condition of employment. Stantec is in compliance with laws and regulations and ensures equitable opportunities in all aspects of employment.

Building an inspired, inclusive work environment that attracts, supports, and develops world-class talent is a crucial key to our success. If you are excited by this role but worry that your experience doesn’t exactly align, we encourage you to apply.

At Stantec we want you to perform your best at every stage of the recruitment process and are committed to ensuring it is accessible to all. If you need any support or require adjustments to be made then please contact careers.UK@stantec.comand we will talk to you about how we can support you.

**ReqID:** 9396

# Head of Fund Accounting

The Fund Accounting team consists of four team members within our London office. The successful candidate will head up the Fund Accounting team and work closely with other support functions. We are looking for someone who knows the role well and can add value straight away. An ideal candidate is one who has a deep understanding of all aspects of fund accounting, a great commercial awareness and is used to multi-tasking and working in a fast-paced and high volume environment.

## Key Responsibilities

* Management of monthly NAV process;
* Ensuring a robust control environment within the Fund Accounting team for the production of daily P&Ls, official estimates, and final monthly NAVS;
* Management of the Fund Accounting team;
* Chairing the Valuation Committee, The HOFA should ensure adherence to the valuation policy and ensure this key document remains up to date, comprehensive, and accurate;
* Producing and reporting of management information both recurring and ad hoc (track record, attribution, scenarios) to stakeholders in the firm, including senior management, client services, and the sales team;
* Management of the regulatory reporting process for the funds;
* Managing the Audited Financial Statements process for the fund entities;
* Management of the service relationships with various outsourced providers, including the external administrator(s) and auditor(s);
* Providing materials for the various governance levels of the firm, e.g.: Corporate Board, Fund Boards, and Executive Committee;
* Managing the internal fund of funds rebalancing processes;
* Managing the FX hedge processes for the funds; and
* Driving forward continuous change as part of the wider finance team thus enabling the firm to continue to innovate and become more scalable and efficient as it continues to grow and add more fund products to investors.

**People Management**

* Holding informal and formal meetings with team members, which includes quarterly one-to-ones and annual appraisals;
* Recruiting and inducting new colleagues;
* Planning, organising, and reviewing the team’s aims, objectives, and priorities on a continual basis;
* Lead and motivate through strong leadership to maximise departmental an individual potential and performance;
* Setting clear standards, expectations, and parameters to encourage a unified team;
* When necessary, effectively manage poor performance for the benefit of the individual, team, and Company; and
* General day-to-day line manager duties such as approving annual leave and managing absence.

## Skills, Knowledge and Expertise

* Employment within an asset management environment;
* A detailed knowledge of fund accounting, involving equalisation credits, contingent redemption, and series accounting is essential and will be discussed at length at interview;
* Adept at discussing and considering hypothetical scenarios and generating ideas with respect to Fund Accounting;
* Excellent communication skills and the ability to interact with all staff at all levels;
* Strong organisational skills and the ability to manage a range of competing priorities and projects to tight deadlines;
* Appropriate IT skillset; and
* Demonstrable and robust people management experience;

**Educational & Professional Qualifications**

* ACA qualified (or equivalent) coupled with a minimum of five years of post-qualification experience; and
* Educated to degree level or higher (or equivalent).

## Benefits

Systematica Investments provides you with excellent benefits from day 1.  We provide private medical insurance for you and your immediate family.  We offer competitive salaries combined with an attractive bonus and pension plus free drinks and snacks at the office.  We also offer paid parental leave with enhanced leave for mothers/primary carers.

# Senior Engineer

Closing Date:
17/10/2026

Contract
Permanent

Job Role
Energy & Renewables

Working Hours
Full Time

Locations
Darlington, Hartlepool, Middlesbrough, Redcar & Cleveland, Stockton-on-Tees

Salary
TBC

Company
Balfour Beatty

#### Job Description

### About the role

Do you want to be at the forefront of one of the world’s most ambitious sustainability initiatives?

Balfour Beatty have created iconic buildings and infrastructure all over the world over the past 115 years redefining excellence and setting the industry benchmark with every project.

As a result, alongside several consortium partners; Balfour Beatty have been selected by bp (British Petroleum) to construct a first-of-a-kind fully integrated gas-fired power station with carbon capture and storage which is a key driving force behind plans to make Teesside the UK’s first decarbonised industrial cluster.

Balfour Beatty is seeking a dynamic **Senior Engineer**to contribute to the **Net Zero Teesside** project based at our new site in **Redcar and Cleveland**.

### What you’ll be doing

As a **Senior Engineer**, you will be responsible for the following:-

* + Supporting the Engineering Manager and Pre-Construction Managers to provide input to the overall design strategy and workload management;

* + Supporting the delivery teams, verifying the work of others in a timely and efficient manner, and providing expert technical support;

* + Providing integration planning of Methods, Permanent and Temporary works with multi disciplinary project delivery teams;

* + Ensuring design risks are considered and prepare design risk assessments. Communicate residual design risks to others;

* + Leading design assurance on projects through conducting regular review meetings with project teams, identifying best practice, areas for improvement and areas of concern;

* + Developing and maintain relationships with relevant technical consultants and suppliers;

* + Promoting the development of BIM within the design process;

* + Supporting the Engineering Manager, in ensuring that learning and best practice is shared across the business stream and the business as a whole;

* + Maintaining personal expertise and knowledge to ensure than Project Engineering is at the forefront of the industry both technically and in using the latest technologies and standards;

* + Carrying out technical audits in the office and site and ensure all actions are closed out;

* + Conform to designer obligations of the Construction (Design and Management) regulations.

### Who we’re looking for

The successful candidate in this role will:

* + have a recognised professional qualification (MICE or MIStructE) and a valid CSCS card;

* + have extensive up to date technical knowledge of temporary works design and ground engineering and industry best practice;

* + be both focussed and thorough and have the gravitas and professional credibility to advise senior management when something needs immediate redress together with the tenacity and drive to ensure that the necessary action is taken;

* + be a subject matter expert with a good understanding in other areas in the engineering field;

* + hold a good working knowledge of mechanical, structural and geotechnical engineering and related software packages and BIM is required;

* + have strong interpersonal and communication skills, coupled with an ability to form effective relationships with partners and delivery team members under time pressure;

* + be customer centric and flexible in approach, with the strategic and creative insight to understand the range of opportunities in invitations to tender and be willing to challenge the norm;

* + know ‘what good looks like’ in submissions and have hands on experience of leading technical aspects in a timely manner;

* + have a desire to continuously pursue innovation and development, with a focus on the customer requirements.

### Why work for us

Our people are our biggest asset and we focus on recruiting, training and developing the people who can apply innovation to deliver the infrastructure of the future. We nurture these talents, offer a great benefits package in addition to a competitive base salary and continually invest in developing the skills of our people at every level.

Some of our key benefits are:

* + An attractive/negotiated salary;

* + Car or car allowance;

* + 25 days annual leave + bank holidays;

* + Pension savings schemes;

* + Enhanced maternity/paternity and family friendly policies;

* + Access to our Refer and Earn scheme;

* + Discretionary annual salary reviews.

### About us

Balfour Beatty’s Major Projects business is delivering some of the UK’s most complex and iconic infrastructure projects. Using the latest technology, we’re driving productivity and creating a lasting legacy by delivering sustainable solutions that strengthen communities.

From consultancy and design, to all aspects of construction and maintenance. We have the proven expertise to deliver large-scale projects safely and successfully.

**Diversity and inclusion**

At Balfour Beatty, we believe that diversity and inclusion are essential components of any successful, happy workplace. Through our Value Everyone Diversity and Inclusion Strategy and Action Plan, we are growing our diverse workforce and developing our inclusive culture where everyone is able to thrive and reach their full potential, regardless of their identity or background. To find out how we are making this a reality, visit www.balfourbeatty.com/diversityandinclusion

To help and support us with our desired commitment to create an inclusive culture we are members of WISE, enei, Business Disability Forum and the Association for Black and Minority Ethnic Engineers (AFBE). In 2020, we signed the Audeliss and Involve Open Letter to demonstrate our commitment to taking key long term and sustainable actions on Black Inclusion. Balfour Beatty is also a Gold Award holder in the Ministry of Defence ‘Employer Recognition Scheme’ and actively encourage applications from Armed Forces personnel, veterans and reservists.

As a Disability Confident Employer, we are committed to working with people who have disabilities and long-term health conditions to remove barriers for them in obtaining employment. We are also committed to offering applicants with a disability an interview if they meet the minimum requirements for the role. For more info, visit: https://disabilityconfident.campaign.gov.uk/
